   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I was wondering if anyone has used spatialite databases in a <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361753951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1L5spdrO2gIbV-2a3ieUkc\">shinyapps.io</a> hosted app. For spatialite to work the lib file (mod_spatialite.dll or mod_spatialite.so) needs to be available and is accessed using the query <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">&quot;</span><span style=\"line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">SELECT load_extension(&#39;mod_spatialite.dll&#39;)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">&quot;. My shiny app was built on a windows machine so I use the .dll version of the query, I expect this is different on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361753951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1L5spdrO2gIbV-2a3ieUkc\">shinyapps.io</a> but I am not sure if it is even available.</span></font></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">thanks in advance...</span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "4Cx7_G6WAAAJ",
   "from": "Tareef Kawaf",
   "author": "edbcc711cdbb3da8",
   "date": "2016-08-01T10:44:26Z",
